---
title: Manifest source boundaries
---
flowchart TB
  accTitle: Manifest source boundaries
  accDescr: A repository is validated into an immutable snapshot and normalized catalog; the application service coordinates installation, while repository-bound trust alone permits the process runner to execute hooks and actions.

  Repo[Git repository]
  User[User]

  subgraph App[Skill Manager boundary]
    Acquire[Source acquisition]
    Snapshot[Immutable commit snapshot]
    Catalog[Normalized catalog]
    Service[Application service]
    IPC[Strict IPC contracts]
    UI[Desktop UI]
    Installer[Transactional installer]
    Trust[(Executable trust store)]
    Ledger[(Installation ledger)]
    Runner[Bounded process runner]
  end

  subgraph UserSpace[Current-user boundary]
    Destinations[Approved destination roots]
    Processes[Source programs and system executables]
  end

  Repo -->|Manifest first| Acquire
  Acquire -->|Retains validated commit| Snapshot
  Snapshot -->|Supplies files and metadata| Catalog
  Catalog --> Service
  User --> UI
  UI --> IPC
  IPC --> Service
  Service --> Installer
  Installer -->|Records ownership and digests| Ledger
  Installer -->|Stages and activates mappings| Destinations
  Trust -->|Allows repository identity| Service
  Service -->|Trusted hooks and explicit actions| Runner
  Runner --> Processes
